Reproduced twice, identically, on two separate location-commit-to-home transitions (01:33:43 and 01:35:... on the Abu Dhabi zone-2 pick-map commit and again on the zone-2 re-pick). Root cause: NEARS-3584 T2's new short-TTL coordinate cache (_reuseZoneResponse) resolves synchronously (no real network await) when a cache hit occurs, so when getZone() is invoked from a widget's initState()/build (e.g. home_screen.dart's non-consumeBootZoneFresh fallback getZone call), the whole _reuseZoneResponse -> _applyZoneEffects -> GetxController.update() chain executes synchronously within the same build phase that triggered it, producing a Flutter "setState() or markNeedsBuild() called during build" FlutterError. Before T2, every getZone call went through _fetchZone which always awaited a real network call, naturally deferring the update() past the current frame.
